    "name": "torus_pocket_spiric_edges",
    "description": "gen1_s11_01829 (seed 11) reduced to the ring and the pocket: the pocket's side walls (vertical planes off the axis) cut the ring's inner fillet torus in 6 spiric sections, which are not conics, so Forge reports them as bspline; the horizontal pocket floor and top cut the torus and cylinder in circles. Regression for the oracle's curve recognition (SPEC-v1 \u00a78.3 rule 3), which at 1e-7 s recognizes some of the short spiric arcs as circles"
